    "summary": "Model built and passed all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nBridge: single simply-supported span, 25 m centre-to-centre of bearings, deck 16 m wide. Five precast prestressed small-box girders per span; middle girder 1.4 m deep, modelled as a 2D spine beam (structure.idealization = spine_beam_2d, structure.system = simply_supported). Supports: abutments at both ends on plain laminated elastomeric bearings, 2 per girder end → 10 bearings/line, modelled as vertical and longitudinal springs (Kv = 1.416e7 kN/m, Kh = 3.28e4 kN/m), rotation free.\n\nRoot cause of the initial failure: the girder section instance had t_top = 0.20 m, contradicting the description's 0.18 m top slab. The accepted section-property decisions had been computed with t_top = 0.18 m, so the rebuilt model's geometry was inconsistent with its provenance decisions and failed L2-1 (and would have failed L3-2, self-weight vs γ·A·L). I corrected the instance to t_top = 0.18 m, which withdrew and required re-accepting girder.single.A/I, girder.A/I, girder.w and girder.m, then re-ran modal analysis and re-decided lane.mu.\n\nKey results (unchanged after the fix, confirming consistency):\n- girder.single.A = 1.0605 m², girder.single.I = 0.2517 m⁴; girder.A = 5.3026 m², girder.I = 1.2583 m⁴ (5 girders).\n- girder.gamma = 26.0 kN/m³ (JTGD60-4.2.1), girder.w = 137.87 kN/m, girder.m = 14.054 t/m.\n- First vertical frequency f1 = 4.272 Hz; impact factor mu = 0.1767 ln(f1) − 0.0157 = 0.241 (JTGD60-4.3.2).\n- Lane loading: 4 lanes, xi = 0.67, qk = 7.875 kN/m², Pk,1 = 232.5 kN.\n- Self-weight reactions 1723.35 + 1723.35 = 3446.7 kN = w × L; midspan self-weight moment 10770.9 kN·m; lane max positive moment 6878.4 kN·m."
